# Russian intonation: statement, question, А ты?
subtitle: "Same words, another tune: how a Russian statement falls and a yes/no question jumps up on the word you ask about."
tags: ["russian","russian intonation","russian pronunciation","questions in russian","trki exam"]
teaches: ["phrases/intonation"]
thumb: "band \"Same words. Question?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"A seventeenth Russian story: the exam","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/170-russian-review-17.cast"}

